---
title: Tempeh egg fried rice
servings: 2
course: dinner
tags: fast, weeknight
source: kitchen idea
time: 20m
---

Dice @tempeh{200%g}, finely chop @onion{1} and mince @garlic{2%clove}. Thinly slice @spring onion{20%g} and keep separate.

Heat a #wok{} over medium-high heat, add @&tempeh{} and fry for ~{4%minutes} until golden, then add @&onion{} and @&garlic{} and cook for ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Push everything to the side of the #&wok{}, crack in @egg{2} and scramble for ~{1%minute}, then add day-old @rice{400%g} and @soy sauce{2%tbsp} and toss for ~{2%minutes} until hot and combined.

Remove from heat, stir through @&spring onion{} and serve immediately.
